          "assignments": [
            { "id": "pk1", "name": "status", "value": "={{ (!$json.busy_dates.includes($json.cand_mon) || !$json.busy_dates.includes($json.cand_tue)) ? 'alternate' : 'none' }}", "type": "string" },
            { "id": "pk2", "name": "requested_date", "value": "={{ $json.requested_date }}", "type": "string" },
            { "id": "pk3", "name": "chosen_date", "value": "={{ !$json.busy_dates.includes($json.cand_mon) ? $json.cand_mon : (!$json.busy_dates.includes($json.cand_tue) ? $json.cand_tue : 'none') }}", "type": "string" }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "finalise",
      "name": "Finalise",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [1340, 460],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            { "id": "fn1", "name": "status", "value": "={{ $json.status }}", "type": "string" },
            { "id": "fn2", "name": "requested_date", "value": "={{ $json.requested_date }}", "type": "string" },
            { "id": "fn3", "name": "chosen_date", "value": "={{ $json.chosen_date }}", "type": "string" },
            { "id": "fn4", "name": "chosen_weekday", "value": "={{ $json.chosen_date === 'none' ? 'n/a' : DateTime.fromISO($json.chosen_date).toFormat('cccc') }}", "type": "string" }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "compose",
      "name": "Compose Reply",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [1560, 460],
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a scheduling assistant. Write a short, friendly reply (2-3 sentences) to someone who asked to meet on {{ $json.requested_date }}. The person prefers Monday or Tuesday afternoons.\n\nFollow the status:\n- confirmed: confirm that {{ $json.requested_date }} works and you look forward to it.\n- alternate: explain that {{ $json.requested_date }} is unfortunately taken, and propose {{ $json.chosen_date }} ({{ $json.chosen_weekday }} afternoon) instead.\n- none: apologise that no Monday or Tuesday afternoon is free in that window, and ask if they can be more flexible.\n\nOutput the reply only — no preamble, no notes.\n\nstatus: {{ $json.status }}\nrequested_date: {{ $json.requested_date }}\nchosen_date: {{ $json.chosen_date }}\nchosen_weekday: {{ $json.chosen_weekday }}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ollama",
      "name": "Ollama Chat Model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOllama",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1560, 660],
      "parameters": { "model": "llama3.1:8b" }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-pattern",
      "name": "Pattern",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [200, 40],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1500,
        "height": 220,
        "color": 7,
        "content": "## Bonus B4 — Check a date, else find an alternate (Reference)\n\nThe routing/gate pattern (Ex 03/04) applied to **dates**. The new skill is n8n's built-in date library, **Luxon** (`DateTime`, `.weekday`, `.plus()`, `.toFormat()`).\n\n```\nRequested date + busy list → Compute Candidates (next Mon & Tue) → Requested Date Free? ─┬─ yes ─→ Confirm ───┐\n                              (Luxon date maths)                  (IF, membership test)  └─ no ──→ Pick Alternate ┴─→ Finalise → Compose Reply (LLM)\n```\n\n**No real calendar, on purpose.** The 'calendar' is a `busy_dates` list. Swapping it for Google Calendar's free/busy node is a credential change, not a logic change — and the logic is the lesson. Dates are computed exactly with expressions; the LLM only writes the human reply."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-luxon",
      "name": "The date maths",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [200, 700],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 900,
        "height": 240,
        "color": 4,
        "content": "## How 'next Monday' is computed\n\n`DateTime.fromISO(requested_date)` parses the date. `.weekday` is **1 = Monday … 7 = Sunday**.\n\nTo jump to the next Monday *strictly after* the requested date:\n`(8 - weekday) % 7 || 7` days. (Monday is weekday 1, and 1 + 7 = 8.)\nFor Tuesday (weekday 2): `(9 - weekday) % 7 || 7`. The `|| 7` forces 'next week' when the requested day already is that weekday, so we never return the same day.\n\n`.plus({ days: N }).toFormat('yyyy-MM-dd')` adds the days and formats back to an ISO date string — same shape as the entries in `busy_dates`, so `.includes()` matches cleanly.\n\n**Why compute, not ask the LLM?** Date arithmetic is exact and auditable in an expression. An LLM doing calendar maths will eventually be wrong. The LLM's only job here is the friendly wording."
      }
    }
  ],
